! IRIX 6.5 colour schemes for mwc's ~/.config/mwc/mwmrc.
! Values: BaseColorPalette at gamma 1.0 (gamma1_0.WMActiveBackground, WMBackground,
! BasicBackground and TextForeground), from the palettes in techomancer/ttr
! (data/schemes/irix). docs/irix-schemes.html shows them as mwc draws them; after a
! change here, make schemes writes it anew.
!
! Use: copy a scheme's four Mwm lines into mwmrc, without the leading "! ". Base
! (= IndigoMagic) is active here. Later lines win, so a scheme further down overrides it.
! mwc's built-in default is none of them: #2e5a8c and #b4b4b4, #c4c4c4 and #000000.
!
! Frames and programs: activeBackground and background are 4Dwm's frame colours.
! basicBackground and textForeground are the colours IRIX's programs drew with; mwc
! draws nothing with them, mtk's clients (deskControl, pulseControl, digitalClock, ...)
! draw on them instead of the frame colours, their text at WCAG's 4.5:1 at least.
! Without basicBackground they keep the frame colours.
!
! Title text: deliberately unset. 4Dwm left it to Motif and so does mwc: black above 70%
! brightness, white otherwise. Where the palette says otherwise, an optional override is
! at the bottom.
!
! The global colours reach programs with frame colours of their own: a global
! activeForeground is their title text too, and unfocused they are mixed with background.
!
! rootBackground is not part of the schemes (IRIX: Customize > Background).
! Without it the desktop keeps mwc's default #5b7792.
! Mwm*rootBackground:          #5b7792

! --- Arizona
! Mwm*activeBackground:        #968d4f
! Mwm*background:              #868373
! Mwm*basicBackground:         #868373
! Mwm*textForeground:          #ffffff

! --- Base  (= IndigoMagic, active)
Mwm*activeBackground:        #c6c1aa
Mwm*background:              #aaaaaa
Mwm*basicBackground:         #d9d9d9
Mwm*textForeground:          #000000

